{
  "$schema": "zenith/words/2",
  "how to use this file": [
    "This is how Zenith guesses where things go. Add the words YOU actually use.",
    "Example: if you work for a client called Northwind, find the \"business\" block",
    "below and add \"northwind\" to its keywords list, in quotes, with a comma.",
    "Same for repo names, project names, nicknames — anything you type a lot.",
    "The \"intent\" blocks below decide what a thing IS. \"pushing\" and \"holding\" are",
    "the two phases of work: pushing has a next action, holding has a standard you",
    "keep level and no deadline. Both live in Work — the guess only sets which",
    "phase it starts in, and ./os push / ./os hold change it any time.",
    "The \"routine\" block at the bottom is different: it is not about where things",
    "go, it is how `./os tidy` notices you are doing something by hand that your",
    "AI could just do. Add the phrases you use for \"I do this every time\".",
    "A \"learned\" list may appear beside \"keywords\" in a block below: those are",
    "words /learn picked up from a subject you studied. They count the same as",
    "yours. Delete any you do not want — nothing writes to your own lists.",
    "Keep the quotes and commas exactly as they are, or the file stops working.",
    "Check it with:  ./os check"
  ],
